    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bīsaltae</span></b> , ārum,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βισάλται</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thracian people on
				the Strymon</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3, 461</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
				29, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">45, 30,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 10, 17, §
			38</span></i>.—Hence <i>the country they
				inhabited</i> was called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bīsaltĭca</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
				29, 6</span></i>, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bī-saltia</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Gell. 16,
			15</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βισαλτία</span>,
		Thuc.).</div>
